# Peer Past the Veil, "Discard your hand. Then draw X cards, where X is the number of card types among cards in your
# graveyard." Turn 1: Bot1 casts Chain Lightning (a sorcery) at Bot2. Turn 2: Bot2 casts Lightning Bolt (an instant) at Bot1, so the
# instant is a type only in the opponent's graveyard. Turn 3: Bot1 casts Peer Past the Veil with Ornithopter and an Island in hand,
# discarding both: the graveyard then holds a sorcery, a land, an artifact and a creature (the Ornithopter has two types) and X is
# 4, counting the discarded cards (the discard comes first), neither Peer Past the Veil itself (an instant, still on the stack,
# CR 608.2n) nor Bot2's Lightning Bolt. Bot1 draws Plains, Forest, Swamp and Mountain.

